      *>---
      *> §2002:7.2.5.1 SR1 - "Compile-time arithmetic expressions shall
      *>   be formed in accordance with 8.8.1, Arithmetic expressions"
      *>   except: a) no exponentiation; b) "All operands shall be
      *>   fixed-point numeric literals"; c) no division by zero and
      *>   "the value of the standard intermediate data item after each
      *>   operation is within the range" of §2002:8.8.1.3.1.1: zero or
      *>   a magnitude from 10**-999 through 10**1000 - 10**968,
      *>   "inclusive, with a precision of 32 decimal digits".
      *>   This program writes the forms SR1 admits; the refused forms
      *>   are g2cta02..g2cta06 in this folder.
      *> EXPECTED OUTPUT, DERIVED (standard arithmetic, §2002:7.2.5.2
      *>   GR1; integer part of the final result, GR2; each product and
      *>   quotient of powers of ten is exact, §2002:8.8.1.3.4/.5):
      *>   C1=001 33 factors 10**30 and one 10**9 give 10**999, the
      *>         largest power of ten inside the range (10**999 <=
      *>         10**1000 - 10**968); dividing back gives 1. A compiler
      *>         with a narrower range (28-digit decimal) refuses C1.
      *>   C2=001 1 divided down to 10**-999, the inclusive lower bound,
      *>         then multiplied back: 1.
      *>   C3=016 fixed-point operands with fractions: 7.5 * 2 = 15,
      *>         0.25 * 4 = 1, 15 + 1 = 16.
      *>   C4=099 100 / 7 = 14.285714285714285714285714285714 (32
      *>         digits, truncated); * 7 = 99.999999999999999999999999
      *>         999998; integer part 99 (GR2). Rounding gives 100.
